# Skill: Inflection Intent

> A Grok skill that reads speech-like inflection plus action words (keep, work, try, do, want, win) to guess true intent.

## Purpose
Explain the skill as a listener for how a line is stressed, not only which words appear. Source: fitzyracing1/skill-inflection-intent.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Read the line.
2. Notice inflection patterns that feel like speech.
3. Notice action keywords.
4. Guess the real ask from both.

## Key ideas
- Inflection (how the line leans)
- Action keywords (keep, work, try, do, want, win)
- True intent (what the speaker is actually asking)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/skill-inflection-intent
inflection = detect(line)
keys = find_action_words(line)
intent = guess(inflection, keys)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. detect(line) → “hear how the line leans”
2. find_action_words(line) → “pick up keep/work/try/do/want/win”
3. guess(...) → “name the real ask”

## Decisions the program makes
- If inflection and keywords agree → use that intent
- If they disagree → prefer the stressed action word

## What a person would notice
The reply follows the lean of the sentence, not only the dictionary meaning.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the HTML skill and drop in one stressed line.
